          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Exterior waterproofing is technically superior because it stops water before it reaches the foundation wall, keeping the wall itself dry and protecting it from deterioration. Interior systems cost roughly half as much and cause far less disruption, but they manage water that has already entered the wall. Choose exterior when the foundation itself is deteriorating, when a block wall is saturating, or during other excavation work; choose interior when the goal is simply a dry, finishable basement.",
